---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Support & Resources — Help for Victims and the Wrongfully Convicted" description="Crisis and victim-support resources, our support for innocence and exoneration work and the wrongfully convicted, and how to share information about a case with law enforcement.">
  <article class="post">
    <p class="evidence evidence--accent">Support &amp; Resources</p>
    <h1>Help for victims — and standing with the wrongfully convicted</h1>
    <div class="post__content">
      <p>Our work follows one rule above every other: help the victims, and never create new ones by helping send an innocent person to prison or ruin a life. These resources are part of that commitment. <strong>If you are in immediate danger, call 911.</strong></p>

      <h2>If you or someone you know needs help</h2>
      <p>These national, confidential resources are available to anyone affected by crime, violence, or crisis. They are free, and most are available 24/7.</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>988 Suicide &amp; Crisis Lifeline</strong> — call or text <strong>988</strong> (24/7).</li>
        <li><strong>RAINN — National Sexual Assault Hotline</strong> — <strong>1-800-656-4673</strong> (24/7); online chat at hotline.rainn.org.</li>
        <li><strong>National Domestic Violence Hotline</strong> — <strong>1-800-799-7233</strong>, or text <strong>START</strong> to <strong>88788</strong> (24/7).</li>
        <li><strong>VictimConnect Resource Center</strong> (National Center for Victims of Crime) — <strong>1-855-484-2846</strong>; help finding services for any crime.</li>
        <li><strong>National Center for Missing &amp; Exploited Children</strong> — <strong>1-800-843-5678</strong> (1-800-THE-LOST).</li>
        <li><strong>Office for Victims of Crime</strong> — find local victim services at ovc.ojp.gov.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Standing with the wrongfully convicted</h2>
      <p>We support the cause of innocence and exoneration work — the use of DNA evidence and post-conviction review to free people who were wrongly convicted, and the reforms in eyewitness identification, interrogation, and forensic science that prevent those errors in the first place. A wrongful conviction is two injustices at once: an innocent person loses their life to a cell, and the person who actually committed the crime stays free. Caring about victims means caring about that, too — it is why presumption of innocence runs through everything we publish.</p>

      <h2>Have information about a case?</h2>
      <p>If you know something about a crime, the people who can act on it are law enforcement — not us. Call <strong>911</strong> for an emergency, contact your <strong>local police department</strong>, or reach the <strong>FBI</strong> at <strong>1-800-CALL-FBI</strong> (1-800-225-5324) or <strong>tips.fbi.gov</strong>. We are grateful to the detectives, forensic scientists, and officers who do the hard, often thankless work of justice.</p>

      <section class="resources" aria-labelledby="reader-resources">
        <h2 id="reader-resources">Victim &amp; Reader Resources</h2>
        <p class="resources__intro">True crime is about real people. If a story on this site touches something in your own life, free and confidential help exists &mdash; and our full, regularly verified resource list now lives in one place on our Stay Safe page.</p>
        <p class="resources__back"><a href="/safety/#immediate-help">Immediate Help and current resources on the Stay Safe page &rarr;</a></p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>

  <style>
    .resources{margin:34px 0 8px;padding-top:26px;border-top:1px solid var(--line)}
    .resources h2{margin-top:0}
    .resources__intro{color:var(--ink-2);max-width:68ch}
    .res{margin:0 0 12px;padding:16px 18px;background:var(--bg-2);border:1px solid var(--line);border-left:3px solid var(--accent);border-radius:8px}
    .res--danger{border-left-color:#d94f3d;background:#1d1512}
    .res__k{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:10.5px;letter-spacing:.16em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--accent);margin:0 0 6px}
    .res--danger .res__k{color:#e8705c}
    .res p{margin:0;line-height:1.6}
    .res__note{margin-top:10px!important;font-size:14px;color:var(--ink-3)}
    .resources__foot{margin:20px 0 0;font-size:14px;color:var(--ink-3);font-style:italic}
    .resources__back{margin:18px 0 0}
    .resources__back a{color:var(--ink-2);font-size:14px;text-decoration:none;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}
    .resources__back a:hover{color:var(--accent)}
  </style>
</Base>
